=== TASK ===
# Department Workspace List

## Overview
You are building a reusable, multi-tenant UI framework for the Connected AI Business OS. This task focuses on the Department Workspace List page: a searchable, filterable catalog of department workspaces available to the current user, each with status indicators and quick metrics. The implementation must adhere to strict runtime safety rules (guard against null/undefined when using arrays, proper defaults, and validated API shapes) and follow a dependency-first ordering: auth and core data setup must precede dashboard/workspace/analytics pages when both are present. The deliverable should include detailed frontend components, backend APIs (even if stubbed for initial pass), data models, and integration guidance, with a cohesive acceptance checklist.

## Page Description (Full Detail)
What this page is:
- The Department Workspace List page presents all department workspaces accessible by the user. Each department is shown as a card with department name, department lead, current headcount, status (active/inactive/paused), and a set of quick KPIs (e.g., open tasks, active users, last activity timestamp).
Goals:
- Provide a fast, filterable, and searchable directory of departments the user can access.
- Communicate access level (you are manager/guest) and provide quick actions per department (open AI assistant, jump to department workspace, view metrics).
- Facilitate admin workflows: create new department workspace (admin only) and configure department-level permissions.
Connected features:
- Linked single department workspace (navigates to dedicated page with overview, team activity, tasks/workflows, docs, and department AI assistant).
- Centralized navigation to the Global Dashboard (for context and role-based shortcuts).
UI elements and how they should look:
- Department cards: display department name, lead, headcount, status badge, and a row of quick metric tiles (e.g., Open Tasks, New Messages, Active Members).
- Search bar: text input with clear action; debounce input; placeholder “Search departments…”.
- Filters:
  - Department type / template (e.g., Sales, Ops, HR, Finance)
  - Status filter (Active, Paused, Inactive)
  - Role-based visibility flags (show only departments user can manage)
- Access controls indicator: small badge or text indicating user role in that department (Manager, Member, Guest).
- Quick link actions: button to Open AI assistant, button to Open department workspace, button to View Details.
- Visual guidance: consistent with the design system, high-contrast typography, dark UI with subtle grid and glass-like panels.
Visual guidance (specific to this project context):
- The color palette, typography, spacing, and card styling described in the Visual Style and UI guidelines must be applied.
- Card hover state: slight lift and soft glow on department card borders.
- KPI tiles: compact, bold numeric values with small uppercase labels.

API integrations:
- No external APIs required for this page in the current scope; all data should be retrieved via the platform’s unified data layer (which you will mock or implement as a local API endpoint for development). The page must be prepared to integrate with the Unified Data and Context Module later.

